|------|-----|
| `EncodedValueUtils.java:90` | Inverted boolean literal: `? 0 : 1` → `? 1 : 0` (true was producing 0/false) |
| `XmlDeobf.java:21` | Added `potentialClassName == null` guard before calling `.indexOf()` |
| `BinaryXMLStrings.java:44` | Changed `id * 4` to `(long) id * 4` to prevent integer overflow in bounds check |
| `BinaryXMLStrings.java:80` | Added bounds check `start >= strArray.length` after `skipStrLen8` to prevent `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` |
| `ResTableBinaryParser.java:211` | Changed `readInt32()` to `readUInt32()` (returning `long`) in `parseTypeSpecChunk` so large chunk sizes aren't sign-extended to negative values |
| `ResTableBinaryParser.java:257` | Clamped cast to `Integer.MAX_VALUE` via `Math.min` before `is.mark()` so oversized chunks don't produce a negative read-limit |
| `BinaryXMLParser.java:524` | Added early `null` return in `deobfClassName()` to prevent NPE when a null-typed attribute value reaches `XmlDeobf` |
| `DecompilerScheduler.java:84` | Wrapped the remaining `mergedBatch` with `Utils.lockList()` so all result batches are consistently immutable |

